# An unclosed `(` does not swallow the query on the next line (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | where f(a
from U | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..35
  PIPELINE@0..18
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..18
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      CALL_EXPR@15..18
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "f"
        ARG_LIST@16..18
          L_PAREN@16..17 "("
          NAME_REF@17..18
            IDENT@17..18 "a"
  WHITESPACE@18..19 "\n"
  PIPELINE@19..34
    IDENT@19..23 "from"
    WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
    NAME_REF@24..25
      IDENT@24..25 "U"
    WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
    PIPE@26..27 "|"
    WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
    TAKE_OP@28..34
      IDENT@28..32 "take"
      WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
      LITERAL@33..34
        LONG@33..34 "1"
  WHITESPACE@34..35 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | from T | where f(a
  |                 ^ this `(` is never closed
2 | from U | take 1
  | ---- expected `)` before this
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
